      "id": 7,
      "purpose": "reference-inherit",
      "direction": "혼합",
      "concept_ko": "[모순] 한 화면 안에서 한쪽은 무너져 비명을 지르는데, 바로 옆 땅은 아무 일 없다는 듯 해가 뜬다 / [남김] ① 그 모순 ② 화면 중앙을 세로로 가르는 좌 어둠–우 빛의 경계 ③ 카메라가 선 자리(바다 쪽에서 반도를 비스듬히 내려다보는 시점) ④ 인물의 화면 내 위치·크기(좌측, 상반신, 화면 높이의 절반) / [바꿈] 피사체(만화체 원형 얼굴 캐릭터 → 푸틴 실명 유화) / 자세·손동작(허공에 뻗은 헛손질 → 관자놀이를 짚은 손, 범주 A) / 관찰 디테일(우크라 표지판 → 물에 반쯤 잠긴 다리 상판 위 그을려 찢긴 삼색기). 좌측은 부정형, 우측은 긍정형. 계승 3장 중 가장 넓은 컷으로 잡아 8·9번과 거리감을 벌린다.",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — that is the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and free of detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags, weapons and key objects sit entirely within the upper five-eighths. Anything held or carried sits at mid height, never near the bottom edge. Style: heavy digital oil painting worked over a photographic base, thick visible brushwork and impasto texture on flags, smoke and fabric, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, every part of the upper five-eighths packed edge to edge with elements and no empty space, cinematic wide-angle, very high contrast, painterly and rough rather than clean — a matte-painting finish, NOT a crisp photo composite, NOT a studio cut-out. Scene: the camera hangs out over the sea and looks down at a slant toward a peninsula, a wide view taking in both shores at once, and the picture divides vertically down the middle. The left half is collapse: black boiling smoke, drifting debris, a burning shoreline, and an enormous Russian tricolour — horizontal white, blue and red bands — filling the left edge from top to bottom, its edges charred black and torn into ragged strips, flame eating along the fabric, soot in every fold, the colours grimy. Standing directly in front of that flag at the far left, painted chest-up and filling about half the frame height, is Vladimir Putin (President of Russia): one palm pressed flat against his own temple, eyes cast down and unfocused toward the water, mouth pulled tight at one corner, his face thrown bright by a raking orange firelight so it separates from the dark. The right half is untouched dawn: the calm bright coastline of the peninsula seen obliquely from offshore, a full gold sunrise breaking over the ridgeline, clear water, and a small intact Ukrainian flag — bright blue band over yellow band, two bands only — flying taut in the wind on the headland. Between the two halves a single column of fire and black smoke rises and forms the boundary; there is no crack and no drawn line. Directly below Putin the sagging severed deck of a causeway lies half-drowned in the shallows with a scorched, torn Russian tricolour trailing off it into the water. Toward the bottom the scene continues into dark smoke and unlit sea with no detail. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "purpose": "reference-inherit",
      "direction": "혼합",
      "concept_ko": "[모순] 한 화면 안에서 한쪽은 무너져 비명을 지르는데, 바로 옆 땅은 아무 일 없다는 듯 해가 뜬다 / [남김] ① 그 모순 ② 화면 중앙을 세로로 가르는 좌 어둠–우 빛의 경계 ③ 카메라가 선 자리(바다 쪽에서 반도를 비스듬히 내려다보는 시점) ④ 인물의 화면 내 위치·크기(좌측, 상반신, 화면 높이의 절반) / [바꿈] 피사체(만화체 원형 얼굴 캐릭터 → 크림 주유소 앞 60대 러시아계 남성 운전자) / 업종·장소(전장 잔해 → 폐쇄된 주유소 앞마당) / 색 온도·광원(석양 골든아워 오렌지 지배 → 청백 여명 냉기 지배 + 낮은 붉은 잔불). 근거는 6월 21일 크림 전역 주유소 일반인 대상 연료 판매 전면 중단, AI-92 차 한 대당 20리터 제한, 암시장 리터당 350루블. 우측 여명 능선에 우크라이나 정찰조 두 명의 얼굴을 밝게 넣어 세트가 러시아 시점으로 닫히지 않게 했다. 중간 거리 컷.",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — that is the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and free of detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags, weapons and key objects sit entirely within the upper five-eighths. Anything held or carried sits at mid height, never near the bottom edge. Style: heavy digital oil painting worked over a photographic base, thick visible brushwork and impasto texture on flags, smoke and fabric, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, every part of the upper five-eighths packed edge to edge with elements and no empty space, cinematic wide-angle, very high contrast, painterly and rough rather than clean — a matte-painting finish, NOT a crisp photo composite, NOT a studio cut-out. Scene: the camera looks down at a slant from over the sea toward the peninsula, the same offshore vantage, and the picture divides vertically down the middle. The left half is a dead petrol station on the coast road before sunrise: canopy lights out, pump islands cold, a queue of abandoned cars behind, everything drowned in cold blue-grey pre-dawn air with only low red embers glowing from a burnt-out generator shed and thin smoke curling up. An enormous Russian tricolour — horizontal white, blue and red bands — hangs from the station canopy and fills the left edge from top to bottom, slack and heavy, its lower edge scorched and torn, soot ground into the folds, the colours sun-bleached and stained. Standing directly in front of it at the far left, painted chest-up and filling about half the frame height, is a Russian man in his sixties in a worn jacket: one hand gripping a dead fuel nozzle at chest height, the other letting an empty twenty-litre jerrycan hang at mid height, jaw slightly slack, eyes searching sideways, deep vertical lines cut between his brows, his face lit by a single hard blue work lamp so it stays bright against the dark. A blank curled sheet of paper with nothing written on it is taped across the pump face. The right half is untouched dawn: the peninsula ridgeline under a clean rising sun, calm bright water below, an intact Ukrainian flag — bright blue band over yellow band, two bands only — flying taut in hard wind on the headland, and two Ukrainian scouts standing on the ridge, small in the frame but with their faces clearly lit and their eyes level and steady. A thin column of smoke rising from the station forms the boundary between the two halves; there is no crack and no drawn line. Toward the bottom the scene continues into dark oil-stained forecourt and ground haze with no detail. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark."
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
