      "direction": "혼합",
      "concept_ko": "[모순] 한 화면 안에서 한쪽은 무너져 비명을 지르는데, 바로 옆 땅은 아무 일 없다는 듯 해가 뜬다 / [남김] ① 그 모순 ② 화면 중앙을 세로로 가르는 좌 어둠–우 빛의 경계 ③ 카메라가 선 자리(바다 쪽에서 반도를 비스듬히 내려다보는 시점) ④ 인물의 화면 내 위치·크기(좌측, 상반신, 화면 높이의 절반) / [바꿈] 피사체(만화체 원형 얼굴 캐릭터 → 50대 러시아군 공병 장교) / 자세·손동작(허공에 뻗은 헛손질 → 손을 화면에서 완전히 뺀 무동작) / 관찰 디테일(우크라 표지판 → 반쯤 가라앉은 부교 잔해). 계승 3장 중 긍정형 전환 컷으로, 우측 여명 능선에 우크라이나 드론 운용병 대열을 크고 밝게 세워 우리 쪽 얼굴이 화면을 받는다. 근거는 대본의 착지점인 '9월 말까지'의 기회의 창과 R-280 화물 71% 감소. 인물을 가장 크게 잡은 얼굴 중심 컷으로 7·8번과 거리감을 벌린다.",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — that is the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and free of detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags, weapons and key objects sit entirely within the upper five-eighths. Anything held or carried sits at mid height, never near the bottom edge. Style: heavy digital oil painting worked over a photographic base, thick visible brushwork and impasto texture on flags, smoke and fabric, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, every part of the upper five-eighths packed edge to edge with elements and no empty space, cinematic wide-angle, very high contrast, painterly and rough rather than clean — a matte-painting finish, NOT a crisp photo composite, NOT a studio cut-out. Scene: the camera looks down at a slant from over the sea toward the peninsula, the same offshore vantage, framed closer than a wide shot so the faces read large, and the picture divides vertically down the middle. The left half is collapse: a wrecked pontoon crossing with its floating sections twisted apart and half sunk, a burnt truck cab tipped into the shallows, black smoke rolling low across the water, and an enormous Russian tricolour — horizontal white, blue and red bands — filling the left edge from top to bottom, its edges charred black and torn into ragged strips, burn holes eaten through the cloth, the colours grimy and desaturated. Standing directly in front of it at the far left, painted chest-up and filling about half the frame height, is a Russian combat-engineer officer in his fifties, mud on his collar, no hands anywhere in the frame: head tipped slightly back, eyes red-rimmed and staring at nothing, lips compressed flat, throat tight, his face pulled bright out of the dark by a low orange firelight. The right half is dawn on the ridge: a clean cold sunrise, an intact Ukrainian flag — bright blue band over yellow band, two bands only — flying large and taut in hard wind with deep folds, and beneath it a column of Ukrainian drone operators receding along the ridgeline, the nearest one framed waist-up, large and sharply lit with a broad hard-set jaw and bright narrowed eyes, one hand steadying a launch rail at chest height, the ones behind him progressively smaller and hazier. A single column of smoke rising from the wrecked crossing forms the boundary between the two halves; there is no crack and no drawn line. Toward the bottom the scene continues into dark water and heavy drifting smoke with no detail. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark."
